urrent/prior rows, dynamically selected connector metrics, derived rates, groupings, and each row’s actual platform. Mixed-platform data MUST NOT inherit one platform classification.\\n\\n#### Scenario: Mixed platforms\\n- GIVEN Meta and Google rows with platform-specific metrics\\n- WHEN the payload is built\\n- THEN both metric sets retain distinct platform identities\\n\\n### Requirement: Safe isolated serialization\\nSerialized values MUST round-trip without loss and MUST prevent account, campaign, creative, or narrative text from executing as HTML or JavaScript. It MUST NOT introduce facts, names, assets, or narratives from an unselected reference company.\\n\\n#### Scenario: Hostile text\\n- GIVEN selected values containing markup and script delimiters\\n- WHEN serialized and embedded\\n- THEN parsing restores them, no code executes, and no reference-client content appears\\n\\n# complete-html-report-export Specification\\n\\n## Purpose\\nDefine four complete downloadable layouts driven only by the report payload.\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Requirement: Four complete layouts\\nThe system MUST provide separate Nutri, Adriana Hoyos, ARTZ, and Shamuna templates. Each MUST reproduce its complete reference structure for available metrics, charts, tables, dates, and generated narratives, not only the export table.\\n\\n#### Scenario: Render all templates\\n- GIVEN one complete payload\\n- WHEN all four options are rendered\\n- THEN four distinct full reports contain every supported section type\\n\\n### Requirement: Payload-only content\\nEvery visible company label, value, date, series, table cell, asset, and narrative MUST derive from the payload. Reports MUST NOT retain reference-company data or reference-only authoring controls.\\n\\n#### Scenario: Replace reference identity\\n- GIVEN account “Acme” and a reference-derived template\\n- WHEN rendered\\n- THEN all company mentions say “Acme” and no reference-client fact remains\\n\\n### Requirement: Hide unavailable sections\\nA template MUST omit sections whose required data remains unavailable after API augmentation. It MUST NOT show unavailable placeholders or fabricated substitutes.\\n\\n#### Scenario: Missing section data\\n- GIVEN a section marked unavailable\\n- WHEN rendered\\n- THEN the section is absent and available sections remain complete\\n\\n### Requirement: Download current HTML\\nThe dashboard MUST download the selected template as valid HTML reflecting the active account, platforms, filters, and data. CSV export and live dashboard behavior MUST remain unchanged.\\n\\n#### Scenario: Changed selection\\n- GIVEN the user changes account, platforms, period, or template\\n- WHEN HTML download is requested\\n- THEN the file has HTML type/name and reflects the new selection\\nSession: dashboard-analytics-reporting-2026-08-04\\nProject: marketing-api\\nScope: project\\nTopic: sdd/full-dashboard-html-templates/spec\\nDuplicates: 1\\nRevisions: 1\\nCreated: 2026-08-17 10:22:07\"}"
