        "text": "{\"project\":\"marketing-api\",\"project_path\":\"/Users/inhaus/Documents/GitHub/marketing-api\",\"project_source\":\"git_remote\",\"result\":\"#478 [architecture] sdd/full-dashboard-html-templates/design\\n# Design: Complete dashboard HTML templates\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\nReplace the generic palette/table exporter with one reporting module and four standalone, reference-shaped HTML templates. `dashboard.py` remains UI orchestration: it captures the active query, passes current/prior frames plus already-fetched optional data, selects a template, and downloads the returned bytes. `dashboard/reporting.py` owns account resolution, lossless normalization, template-specific API augmentation, derived data, availability, safe serialization, and file loading.\\n\\n## Architecture Decisions\\n\\n| Decision | Alternatives / tradeoff | Choice and rationale |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Rendering boundary | Python-generated HTML is easier to assert but would recreate four large documents in Python; patching reference strings can leak client facts. | Four HTML files plus one injected JSON payload preserve each layout and keep Python small without a new template dependency. |\\n| Metric preservation | Changing existing canonical columns risks the live dashboard; relying on them loses connector-specific fields. | Extend `process_api_response()` with immutable `source_platform` and the original `source_metrics` dictionary while retaining every current column. Reporting reads exact source metrics; zero is available, absence is not. |\\n| Multi-platform identity | Current code uses the first selected platform. | Cache every platform/account query config and group by `source_platform`; never infer all rows from `platform_configs[0]`. |\\n| Account naming | Labels containing only IDs or the first account can misidentify reports. | Resolve each selected connection through `account_name → name → display_name`; use an explicit platform/account fallback. Join distinct selected names deterministically for mixed-account reports. |\\n| Fallback | Eagerly requesting every schema metric is slow; merging supplemental rows can double-count. | For the chosen template, reuse primary/export/optional data, then request only missing schema-supported metric/dimension batches through existing `dashboard.api` functions with errors suppressed. Keep supplemental datasets separate and select one source per metric. Failed/empty calls set availability false. |\\n| Safety and assets | `innerHTML` and copied reference embeds are unsafe; ARTZ also has 14 broken paths. | Embed JSON in `\\u003cscript type=\\\"application/json\\\"\\u003e` with `\\u003c`, `\\u003e`, `\\u0026`, U+2028/U+2029 escaped. Templates use `textContent`, numeric chart inputs, and allowlisted HTTPS asset URLs. Copy no reference facts, logos, creative paths, PIN controls, or nested exporters. |\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n    active Streamlit query\\n      ├─ current/prior frames + CSV/display table\\n      ├─ all account/platform configs\\n      └─ optional breakdowns/rankings/previews\\n                    │\\n                    ▼\\n    build_report_payload(template)\\n      ├─ normalize exact source metrics\\n      ├─ fetch only missing supported data\\n      └─ compute summaries, deltas, series, tables,\\n         deterministic narratives, and availability\\n                    │\\n                    ▼\\n    safe JSON → selected standalone HTML → download\\n\\nA template-local section is initially hidden and becomes visible only when its exact availability key is true; otherwise JavaScript removes it. Parent panels disappear when no child remains. Competition, plans, targets, invoices, strategy, or CRO content therefore stays absent unless current/API data actually supplies its required facts.\\n\\n## File Changes\\n\\n| File | Action | Description |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `dashboard.py` | Modify | Remove generic renderer; retain all active account configs and pass report inputs/optional datasets to reporting. |\\n| `dashboard/api.py` | Modify | Preserve `source_platform` and lossless `source_metrics`. |\\n| `dashboard/reporting.py` | Create | Payload builder, fallback, aggregation, narratives, URL validation, JSON escaping, and allowlisted template loader. |\\n| `dashboard/report_templates/nutri.html` | Create | Complete Nutri-shaped conditional report. |\\n| `dashboard/report_templates/adriana_hoyos.html` | Create | Complete Adriana Hoyos-shaped conditional report. |\\n| `dashboard/report_templates/artz.html` | Create | Complete ARTZ-shaped report without broken reference assets. |\\n| `dashboard/report_templates/shamuna.html` | Create | Complete Shamuna-shaped conditional report. |\\n| `tests/test_dashboard_exports.py` | Modify | Assert the new dashboard integration without source-string extraction of the removed function. |\\n| `tests/test_dashboard_reporting.py` | Create | Contract, fallback, safety, isolation, and four-template coverage. |\\n\\n## Interfaces / Contracts\\n\\n`build_report_payload(template_name, current, previous, export_table, query_context, optional, client_id, user_id, api_key) -\\u003e dict`\\n\\nPayload groups: `meta`, `rows.current/prior/supplemental`, `summary`, `deltas`, `by_platform`, `daily_series`, `breakdowns`, `tables`, `narratives`, and `availability`. No credential enters the payload.\\n\\n`render_report(template_name, payload) -\\u003e str` accepts only the four mapping keys, loads the corresponding file relative to `reporting.py`, replaces one data marker, and fails closed for unknown or malformed templates.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n| Layer | Coverage |\\n|---|---|\\n| Unit | Named/unnamed/multiple accounts; mixed platforms; dynamic metrics; valid zero; divide-by-zero; fallback called only for missing supported data; failure hides sections; hostile text round-trip; unsafe URLs rejected. |\\n| Integration | Render all four templates from one fixture; verify distinct landmarks, active dates/accounts/tables, no reference facts/assets, valid HTML parsing, and unchanged CSV behavior. |\\n| Browser visual QA | Generate each file, open with agent-browser, check desktop/mobile screenshots, hidden sections, chart/table rendering, console errors, and no broken ARTZ requests. |\\n\\n## Threat Matrix\\n\\nN/A — no routing, shell, subprocess, VCS/PR automation, executable classification, or process integration boundary.\\n\\n## Migration / Rollout\\n\\nNo data migration. Implement the contract first, then one template per review slice because the reference-derived HTML exceeds the 400-line review budget. Existing CSV and live dashboard remain the rollback path.\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\nNone.\\nSession: dashboard-analytics-reporting-2026-08-04\\nProject: marketing-api\\nScope: project\\nTopic: sdd/full-dashboard-html-templates/design\\nDuplicates: 1\\nRevisions: 1\\nCreated: 2026-08-17 10:27:42\"}"
